#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""review-gate — the two halves of /finish step 1 that are code, not judgement. Stdlib, Python 3.9.

    review-gate plan  [--base main] [--json]
        Which two reviews this branch gets: counts inserted lines in `git diff base...HEAD` and
        reads the week's plan usage, then names the agents and the `/code-review` level.
    review-gate merge --reviewer FILE --code-review FILE [--repo DIR] [--base main] [--no-model] [--no-shadow]
        One de-duplicated, severity-sorted list from the two reports. Prints Markdown.

Design: docs/record/review-gate-2026-10-02.md (the owner's D1–D7), from the bench in
docs/record/review-codereview-bench-2026-09-30.md. The proposal called the merge `bin/review-merge`;
it lives here beside `plan` so /finish calls one script.

plan — the size rule (D7), counted in INSERTED lines (deletions moved C11 to the wrong tier):
  under 100        reviewer at high  + /code-review high
  100 to 1,000     reviewer at high  + /code-review xhigh
  over 1,000       reviewer at xhigh + /code-review xhigh
  The path rule (docs/autofinish-exclude-2026-10-23.md S5, approved 2026-10-23): a branch that changes
  a path under the base's `autofinish_exclude` or `review_xhigh` (.claude/workflow.json at <base>, never
  the branch's copy; classes 1 to 3, and `review_xhigh` keeps class 3 there once S6 takes it off the
  list) gets the top tier whatever its size: a one-line hook change is the reading that lets a judge or
  a hook land without a person's tap. The week lowers it as it lowers the top tier.
  The week, from hooks/tier_check.py (the same reading and threshold the session's tier line
  uses): "tight" (10 points over pace, or 80% used) turns the top tier into xhigh + CR high;
  "lowest" (LOWEST% used, a threshold set here, not measured) puts every tier on high + CR high
  (TODO 12's wording). The reviewer's effort lives in agent frontmatter and the Agent tool cannot
  set it, so each level is its own agent file: reviewer (xhigh) / reviewer-high, bodies kept
  identical by bin/test_review_gate.sh. A project with its own `reviewer` and no `reviewer-high`
  (the home repo) keeps its own at its own effort: its read-only probe list matters more than the
  effort. /code-review needs no second agent: a forked skill takes its effort from the level in
  its args (Claude Code 2.1.287 source, "SkillTool executing forked skill"), so one
  `code-reviewer` passes the level and its own effort only prices its two turns.
  The week reading is dropped when sampled before the current week began (a stale cache keeps
  last week's percent while the reset rolls forward).
  Each review's provider is a row in settings/models.json (review-gate.reviewer,
  review-gate.code-review), read through bin/gate: plan prints it and refuses a provider it has
  no agent for (claude only, today); a row off with when_off skip prints "off" and names no agent.

merge — G4 of the Jev pipeline doc:
  1. Parse: the reviewer's blocks (`file:line — text` then `verdict:`) and /code-review's JSON
     list (the last fenced block, or the whole text).
  2. Pair in code: every reviewer finding against every /code-review finding on the same file.
  3. One call on the review-gate.merge row (Opus 5.5 `medium` today; `claude -p`, no tools, no
     settings) answers "same defect?" per pair and a severity per finding; the row off is --no-model. B2 measured precision 0.90, recall 0.93 on 1,090 pairs, but
     with its own prompts (pairs batched 15 a call; severity from the diff hunk): this combined
     prompt, with severity from the claim alone, is unmeasured. p >= 0.5 merges. On any failure the lists come out unmerged, unsorted by severity, and say so:
     the gate never blocks /finish.
  4. Check each cited file:line exists in the worktree (code, not a model, as G4 asked).
  5. Jev (D4): the review-gate.same-shadow row (Jev, `batch: 1`) answers the same pairs, one
     classify call per pair as B2 measured, in parallel with the merge call. Two weeks in shadow
     met D4's bar (verdict 2026-10-19: 0 of 1,544 confident pairs disagreed with Opus, against
     0.5% allowed; the band 51.8%, against 40% — the record's "Checked, 2026-10-19"), so since then Jev's answer decides a
     pair it is confident on (p < 0.1 or > 0.9) and Opus's the rest — only from a model in TAKES,
     the version measured; a newer Jev is shadow again until re-measured. Both answers still go
     to the log, which says who decided each pair. Through bin/gate's classify, never from a
     hook; a repo bin/jev guards (the registry's guarded list) is refused by the gate and skipped,
     not sent; the row off logs "shadow off"; a Jev error leaves the pair to Opus.
  The parent still checks every finding against the code with its tools before fixing it (D5:
  no cheap model can judge a finding).

Log: one JSON line per merge in $REVIEW_GATE_LOG, default <data>/review-gate.jsonl, where <data> is
bin/usage-report's own (usage.json's "data" for this host; the log dir on both Macs today),
local, not git: repo, branch, counts, cost, and per pair both scores and the two claims cut to
300 characters — D4 reads disagreements one by one, as the bench did.
Since 2026-10-05 the line also carries the passive quality metrics of the model-routing design
(docs/record/model-routing-2026-09-30.md section 7, D8; S-E), read by `usage-report numbers`:
  diff      added and removed lines against --base, doc files left out (DOC_RE);
  findings  the merged list's items by severity (S1, S2, S3, S? when the merge model did not run);
  wrong     the same for the confirmed ones: an item holding a reviewer `WRONG` (the reviewer checked
            it against the code; a /code-review finding alone is unconfirmed, D5);
  models    who built the branch, read from its transcripts, never from a brief: the main sessions'
            models (assistant records whose gitBranch is this branch) and each subagent's type (its
            meta file) and model (its own records; the meta's `model` is only the alias asked for).
            A subagent counts when its records are on the branch, or when its parent session was on
            the branch at the time it started — a worker in its own worktree carries its own branch.
            Only records in this repo count (cwd, a worktree mapped to its main checkout), and the
            agents of the review itself (REVIEW_SKILLS: /finish's reviewers, the forked /code-review)
            are left out: they reviewed the branch, they did not build it.
"""
import argparse
import concurrent.futures as cf
import glob
import json
import os
import re
import queue
import subprocess
import sys
import threading
import time
from importlib.machinery import SourceFileLoader

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
# The core (lib/core_path.py, C2) and its gate: a hard edge, so none found is one line and exit 2.
# usage-report and tier_check are peers (plumb), found through common.tool() and optional (G7).
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(HERE, "..", "lib"))
import core_path  # noqa: E402
CORE_HOOKS = core_path.require()
import common  # noqa: E402
# The core's own gate, beside the hooks require() found — not tool("gate"), which searches every
# module and returns None (the path "None") where the registry's scope hides the core.
gate = SourceFileLoader("gate", os.path.join(CORE_HOOKS, "..", "bin", "gate")).load_module()
SMALL, LARGE = 100, 1000   # inserted lines (D7)
LOWEST = 90                # % of the week used: every tier drops to high + CR high
SAME = 0.5
CONFIDENT = (0.1, 0.9)     # Jev decides a pair below the first or above the second (D4's band)
TAKES = ("jev-1.13.0",)    # the Jev versions D4's shadow measured: only these decide a pair
SHADOW_DEADLINE = 90       # s for the whole Jev shadow
OPUS_TIMEOUT = 420         # s for the merge call; /finish gives the command 600
DOC_RE = re.compile(r"(\.(md|markdown|txt|rst)$|(^|/)docs/)")
TRANSCRIPTS = ("USAGE_CC", "~/.claude/projects"), ("USAGE_ARCHIVE", "~/projects/transcripts")  # usage-report's


def peer(name, as_name):
    """A peer module's tool loaded as a module (G7). Absent: an error that names it, which each
    caller's `except` turns into its fallback."""
    p = common.tool(name)
    if not p:
        raise FileNotFoundError("%s not installed" % name)
    return SourceFileLoader(as_name, str(p)).load_module()


def log_path():
    if os.environ.get("REVIEW_GATE_LOG"):
        return os.environ["REVIEW_GATE_LOG"]
    try:
        ur = peer("usage-report", "usage_report")
        return str(ur.data_dir() / "review-gate.jsonl")
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 — the log must still be written somewhere: the core's log dir
        print("review-gate: usage data folder not read (%s); log in %s" % (e, common.LOG_DIR), file=sys.stderr)
        return str(common.LOG_DIR / "review-gate.jsonl")

# ---------- plan ----------


def git(repo, *args):
    p = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", repo] + list(args), capture_output=True, text=True)
    return p.stdout if p.returncode == 0 else ""


def inserted(repo, base):
    """-> (inserted lines, warning or None). A failed diff is said, never read as 0 lines."""
    p = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", repo, "diff", "--numstat", "%s...HEAD" % base],
                       capture_output=True, text=True)
    if p.returncode != 0:
        return 0, "git diff %s...HEAD failed (%s): the tier below is a guess" % (base, p.stderr.strip()[:120])
    n = 0
    for line in p.stdout.splitlines():
        a = line.split("\t", 1)[0]
        if a.isdigit():  # "-" for a binary file
            n += int(a)
    return n, (None if p.stdout.strip() else "no difference from %s: is this the branch's worktree?" % base)


def gated_path(repo, base):
    """The first path `base...HEAD` changes under the base's `autofinish_exclude` or `review_xhigh`, or
    None. A list that will not read is no path: the size rule still holds, and the landing's own gates
    (bin/autofinish, bin/pr) judge the list; this only prices the review."""
    show = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", repo, "show", "%s:.claude/workflow.json" % base],
                          capture_output=True, text=True)
    try:
        cfg = json.loads(show.stdout) if show.returncode == 0 else {}
    except ValueError:
        cfg = {}
    prefixes = tuple(p for key in ("autofinish_exclude", "review_xhigh")
                     for p in (cfg.get(key) if isinstance(cfg, dict) and isinstance(cfg.get(key), list) else [])
                     if isinstance(p, str) and p)
    if not prefixes:
        return None
    d = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", repo, "-c", "core.quotePath=false", "diff", "--name-only", "--no-renames",
                        "%s...HEAD" % base], capture_output=True, text=True)
    return next((f for f in sorted(d.stdout.splitlines()) if f.startswith(prefixes)), None) if d.returncode == 0 else None


def week():
    """-> (percent, pace, ahead, low, age in hours) or None, through tier_check's own reading."""
    try:
        tc = peer("tier_check.py", "tier_check")
        w = tc.weekly(tc.load(tc.CLAUDE_JSON))
        if not w:
            return None
        age = (tc.now() - w[1] / 1000) / 3600
        if not w[2]:  # no reset time: no pace, but the 80%-used rule still holds
            return float(w[0]), None, tc.AHEAD, tc.LOW, age
        if w[1] / 1000 < w[2] - tc.WEEK:  # sampled before this week began: last week's percent
            print("review-gate: week reading predates this week's reset; ignored", file=sys.stderr)
            return None
        return float(w[0]), tc.week_pace(w[2]), tc.AHEAD, tc.LOW, age
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 — no week reading means the normal tiers
        print("review-gate: week not read (%s)" % e, file=sys.stderr)
        return None


def own_reviewer(repo):
    """A project's own reviewer without a -high twin is used as is (the home repo's AGENTS.md)."""
    d = os.path.join(repo, ".claude", "agents")
    return os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, "reviewer.md")) and not os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, "reviewer-high.md"))


def review_provider(site):
    """The provider a review row names, None when it is off + skip. GateError (GateOff too) for a
    row plan cannot run: /finish's review agents are Claude Code agents, so claude only, today."""
    row = gate.resolve(site)
    if row is not None and row["provider"] != "claude":
        raise gate.GateError("%s: provider %s has no review agent here (claude only) — `bin/gate set %s "
                             "provider=claude`, or write its agent first" % (site, row["provider"], site))
    return row and row["provider"]


def plan(repo, base):
    rp, cp = review_provider("review-gate.reviewer"), review_provider("review-gate.code-review")
    n, warn = inserted(repo, base)
    w = week()
    budget = "normal"
    if w:
        pct, pace, ahead, low, _ = w
        if pct >= LOWEST:
            budget = "lowest"
        elif (pace is not None and pct > pace + ahead) or pct >= low:
            budget = "tight"
    gated = gated_path(repo, base)
    if n < SMALL:
        tier, r, c = "small", "high", "high"
    elif n <= LARGE:
        tier, r, c = "medium", "high", "xhigh"
    else:
        tier, r, c = "large", "xhigh", "xhigh"
    if gated:   # the path rule: the top tier at any size
        r, c = "xhigh", "xhigh"
    if r == "xhigh" and budget == "tight":
        c = "high"
    if budget == "lowest":
        r, c = "high", "high"
    rev = {"agent": "reviewer" if r == "xhigh" else "reviewer-high", "effort": r}
    if own_reviewer(repo):
        rev = {"agent": "reviewer", "effort": "the project's own"}
    rev["provider"] = rp or "off"
    cr = {"agent": "code-reviewer", "level": c, "args": "%s %s...HEAD" % (c, base), "provider": cp or "off"}
    for x, on in ((rev, rp), (cr, cp)):
        if not on:
            x["agent"] = None
    return {
        "inserted": n, "tier": tier, "budget": budget, "warning": warn, "gated": gated,
        "week": {"percent": w[0], "pace": w[1], "age_h": round(w[4], 1)} if w else None,
        "reviewer": rev,
        "code_review": cr,
    }


def print_plan(p):
    w = p["week"]
    wk = ("week %.0f%% (pace %s, sampled %.1f h ago), %s" % (
        w["percent"], "%.1f%%" % w["pace"] if w["pace"] is not None else "unknown", w["age_h"], p["budget"])
        if w else "week unknown, normal")
    if p["warning"]:
        print("⚠ " + p["warning"])
    print("size: %d inserted lines → %s tier · %s" % (p["inserted"], p["tier"], wk))
    if p.get("gated"):
        print("path: %s is on the base's autofinish_exclude → the top tier at any size" % p["gated"])
    off = "off in settings/models.json — not spawned"
    r, c = p["reviewer"], p["code_review"]
    print("reviewer:    " + ("subagent_type %s (effort: %s), provider %s, model opus" % (r["agent"], r["effort"], r["provider"])
                             if r["agent"] else off))
    print("code-review: " + ("subagent_type code-reviewer, provider %s, model opus, prompt: %s" % (c["provider"], c["args"])
                             if c["agent"] else off))


# ---------- merge: parse ----------

# Real heads vary (a 2026-10-02 sweep of 9 reviewer reports lost 21 of 74 blocks to a strict
# pattern): `a.py:241-257, 294 — …`, `a.py:280 + b.yaml:19 — …`, `a.py (this branch) — …`,
# `dir/*.yaml — …`. So a block is anchored on its verdict line and never dropped: the first
# path-like token gives file and line when there is one, else file "?" and the whole head.
VERDICT_RE = re.compile(r"(?i)^\W*verdict\W*:\W*([A-Z][A-Z-]*)")
FIELD_RE = re.compile(r"(?i)^\W*(evidence|fix)\W*:\W*(.*)")
PATH_RE = re.compile(r"(?P<file>[\w.*-]*[/.][\w./*-]*\w)(?::(?P<line>\d+))?")
DASH_RE = re.compile(r"\s+(?:—|–|--|-)\s+")


def parse_reviewer(text):
    """-> (findings, number of verdict lines). Head line, then verdict/evidence/fix lines."""
    lines = text.splitlines()
    out, seen = [], 0
    for i, l in enumerate(lines):
        m = VERDICT_RE.match(l)
        if not m:
            continue
        seen += 1
        j = i - 1
        while j >= 0 and (not lines[j].strip() or lines[j].strip().startswith("```")):
            j -= 1
        head = lines[j].strip().strip("`*").strip() if j >= 0 else ""
        parts = DASH_RE.split(head, 1)
        if len(parts) == 2:
            parts[0] = parts[0].strip("`* ")
        pm = PATH_RE.search(parts[0]) if len(parts) == 2 else PATH_RE.match(head)
        f = dict(file=pm.group("file").strip("`*") if pm else "?",
                 line=int(pm.group("line")) if pm and pm.group("line") else None,
                 text=(parts[1] if len(parts) == 2 else head).strip() or "(no head line)",
                 verdict=m.group(1).upper())
        if len(parts) == 2 and parts[0] != (pm.group(0) if pm else ""):
            f["cites"] = parts[0].strip("`* ")  # several places, a range, a note: kept as written
        field = None
        for k in range(i + 1, len(lines)):
            if VERDICT_RE.match(lines[k]) or (k + 1 < len(lines) and VERDICT_RE.match(lines[k + 1])):
                break
            km = FIELD_RE.match(lines[k])
            if km:
                field = km.group(1).lower()
                f[field] = km.group(2).strip()
            elif field and lines[k].strip() and not lines[k].strip().startswith("```"):
                f[field] += " " + lines[k].strip()  # a field's continuation lines
            elif not lines[k].strip():
                field = None
        out.append(f)
    return out, seen


def parse_code_review(text):
    m = re.findall(r"```(?:json)?\s*\n(.*?)\n```", text, re.S)
    try:
        items = json.loads(m[-1] if m else text)
    except ValueError:
        return None
    if isinstance(items, dict):
        items = items.get("findings")
    if not isinstance(items, list):
        return None
    out = []
    for x in items:
        if not isinstance(x, dict):
            continue
        try:
            line = int(x.get("line")) if x.get("line") is not None else None
        except (TypeError, ValueError):
            line = None
        out.append(dict(file=x.get("file") or "?", line=line, text=(x.get("summary") or "").strip(),
                        scenario=(x.get("failure_scenario") or "").strip(), category=x.get("category")))
    return out


def norm(repo, f):
    f = (f or "").strip()
    if os.path.isabs(f) and repo and f.startswith(repo.rstrip("/") + "/"):
        f = os.path.relpath(f, repo)
    while f.startswith("./"):  # never lstrip("./"): it eats a dotfile's dot
        f = f[2:]
    return f


# ---------- merge: models ----------

PROMPT = """You merge two code-review reports on one change. The FINDINGS are labelled R (the project
reviewer) and C (the code-review skill). Answer two things, judging each on its own:

severity, for every finding: 0 for a doc, naming, comment or style issue; 1 for wrong behaviour of
the software; 2 for physical, irreversible, data loss or an unwanted write to a live system (say
what it would be if true).
same, for every PAIR: the probability (0 to 1) that a and b describe the same underlying defect:
fixing one would also resolve the other (same place in the code, same problem), not merely the
same file or nearby lines.

Return only one JSON object: {"severity": {"<finding id>": 0|1|2, ...}, "same": {"<pair id>": <0..1>, ...}}

FINDINGS:
%s

PAIRS:
%s"""


def claim(f):
    s = f["text"]
    if f.get("scenario"):
        s += " — " + f["scenario"]
    return s


def model_label(row):
    """The header's short name for a row: claude-opus-5-5 (or opus) at medium is "Opus medium"."""
    m = re.sub(r"^claude-", "", row.get("model") or "").split("-")[0].capitalize() or row["provider"]
    return " ".join(x for x in (m, row.get("effort")) if x)


def ask_merge(findings, pairs, repo, row):
    body_f = "\n".join(json.dumps({"id": f["id"], "file": f["file"], "line": f["line"], "claim": claim(f)},
                                  ensure_ascii=False) for f in findings)
    body_p = "\n".join("%s: a=%s b=%s" % (p["id"], p["a"], p["b"]) for p in pairs) or "(none)"
    # CLAUDE_BIN as bin/gate reads it: a suite names its stand-in by path, so a failed exec of it can
    # never fall through to a real `claude` later on PATH (which answers "Not logged in")
    cmd = [os.environ.get("CLAUDE_BIN", "claude"), "-p", *gate.claude_flags(row), "--output-format", "json",
           "--tools", "", "--setting-sources", "", "--no-session-persistence"]
    env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k != "CLAUDECODE"}
    p = subprocess.run(cmd, input=PROMPT % (body_f, body_p), cwd=repo or None, env=env,
                       capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=OPUS_TIMEOUT)
    try:
        res = json.loads(p.stdout)
    except ValueError:
        raise RuntimeError("no JSON from claude -p: %s" % (p.stdout + p.stderr)[-300:])
    if res.get("is_error"):
        raise RuntimeError(str(res.get("result"))[:300])
    txt = res.get("result") or ""
    m = re.findall(r"```(?:json)?\s*\n(.*?)\n```", txt, re.S)
    ans = json.loads(m[-1] if m else txt)
    return ans.get("severity") or {}, ans.get("same") or {}, float(res.get("total_cost_usd") or 0)


# bench/b2.py's question and criteria, word for word; the request shape is bin/gate's, not B2's (TODO 10).
SHADOW = "review-gate.same-shadow"
ASK_SAME = "Do `a` and `b`, two code-review findings on the same change, describe the same underlying defect?"
LABELS_SAME = {
    "yes": "fixing the defect in one would also resolve the other: same place in the code, same problem",
    "no": "they are different problems, even if they touch the same file or nearby lines",
}
VENDOR_NAME = {"jev": "TypeSafe", "claude": "Anthropic", "codex": "OpenAI"}


def shadow(byid, pairs, source):
    """The shadow row on every pair; ({pair id: {p, label, model, cost_usd} | {error}}, note). Never raises."""
    if not pairs:
        return {}, None
    try:
        row = gate.resolve(SHADOW)
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 — a bad table must not hold up /finish
        return {}, "shadow not run: %s" % e
    if row is None:
        return {}, "shadow off (settings/models.json %s)" % SHADOW
    who = "%s shadow" % row["provider"].capitalize()

    out, refused, todo = {}, [], queue.Queue()
    for p in pairs:
        todo.put(p)

    def worker():
        while True:
            try:
                p = todo.get_nowait()
            except queue.Empty:
                return
            item = {k: {"file": byid[p[k]]["file"], "line": str(byid[p[k]]["line"] or ""), "claim": claim(byid[p[k]])}
                    for k in ("a", "b")}
            try:
                r = gate.classify(SHADOW, {p["id"]: item}, ASK_SAME, LABELS_SAME, source=source,
                                  caller="review-gate", timeout=10, attempts=1)
                if r is None:  # flipped off mid-run
                    out[p["id"]] = {"error": "off"}
                    continue
                a = r["items"][p["id"]]
                out[p["id"]] = {"p": a["p"], "label": a["label"], "model": r.get("model"), "cost_usd": r["cost_usd"]}
            except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 — a pair Jev did not answer is Opus's
                if isinstance(e, gate.GateError) and ": refused: " in str(e):
                    refused.append(p["id"])  # a guarded repo: the gate sent nothing
                out[p["id"]] = {"error": str(e)[:200]}

    # Daemon threads and a total deadline: a hung TypeSafe must not hold up /finish, and Opus
    # answers every pair anyway (unfinished pairs are logged as "deadline" and stay Opus's).
    ts = [threading.Thread(target=worker, daemon=True) for _ in range(8)]
    for t in ts:
        t.start()
    end = time.time() + SHADOW_DEADLINE
    for t in ts:
        t.join(max(0, end - time.time()))
    if refused:
        return {}, "%s skipped: %s is not sent to %s" % (who, source, VENDOR_NAME.get(row["provider"], row["provider"]))
    late = [p["id"] for p in pairs if p["id"] not in out]
    res = dict(out)
    for k in late:
        res[k] = {"error": "deadline"}
    return res, ("%s: %d pair(s) past the %d s deadline" % (who, len(late), SHADOW_DEADLINE) if late else None)


# ---------- merge: what the log line measures (S-E) ----------


def diff_size(repo, base):
    """{added, removed} lines against base, doc files left out; None when the diff fails."""
    p = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", repo, "diff", "--numstat", "%s...HEAD" % base], capture_output=True, text=True)
    if p.returncode != 0:
        return None
    a = r = 0
    for line in p.stdout.splitlines():
        parts = line.split("\t")
        if len(parts) < 3 or not parts[0].isdigit() or DOC_RE.search(parts[2].rstrip("}")):
            continue
        a, r = a + int(parts[0]), r + int(parts[1])
    return {"added": a, "removed": r, "base": base}


def _assistant(path, need=None):
    """The assistant records of one transcript; with `need`, only lines holding that text."""
    try:
        fh = open(path, errors="replace")
    except OSError:
        return
    with fh:
        for line in fh:
            if '"assistant"' not in line or (need and need not in line):
                continue
            try:
                d = json.loads(line)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            model = (d.get("message") or {}).get("model")
            if d.get("type") == "assistant" and model and model != "<synthetic>" and d.get("timestamp"):
                yield d


# Skills whose agents review a branch rather than build it: /finish spawns the reviewers, and the
# forked /code-review runs as general-purpose under its own skill name (review 2026-10-05).
REVIEW_SKILLS = {"finish", "code-review"}


def _home(cwd):
    """The main checkout a record's cwd belongs to: a worktree under .claude/worktrees/ counts as its repo."""
    return cwd.split("/.claude/worktrees/", 1)[0].rstrip("/") if cwd else None


def built_by(branch, home=None):
    """The models that built `branch`, from its transcripts (see the module docstring), or None.
    With `home` (the repo's main checkout), only records whose cwd is in that repo count: branch
    names repeat across repos (11 of 420 did on 2026-10-05)."""
    if not branch or branch == "HEAD":
        return None
    m = re.search(r"\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}", branch)
    try:
        since = time.mktime(time.strptime(m.group(0), "%Y-%m-%d")) - 2 * 86400 if m else time.time() - 30 * 86400
    except ValueError:
        since = time.time() - 30 * 86400
    need = json.dumps(branch)  # a prefilter only; the parsed gitBranch decides
    mains, subs = [], []
    for env, default in TRANSCRIPTS:
        root = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get(env) or default)
        for f in glob.glob(os.path.join(root, "**", "*.jsonl"), recursive=True):
            try:
                if os.path.getmtime(f) < since:
                    continue
            except OSError:
                continue
            (subs if os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(f)) == "subagents" else mains).append(f)
    main, timeline = {}, {}
    for f in mains:
        if not any(True for _ in _assistant(f, need)):
            continue
        # The whole session, every branch: a subagent belongs to the branch its parent was on when
        # it started, and a parent that stepped onto another branch in between was not on this one.
        for d in _assistant(f):
            if d.get("isSidechain") or (home and _home(d.get("cwd")) != home):
                continue
            timeline.setdefault(d.get("sessionId"), []).append((d["timestamp"], d.get("gitBranch")))
            if d.get("gitBranch") == branch:
                main[d.get("requestId") or d.get("uuid")] = d["message"]["model"]
    for t in timeline.values():
        t.sort()

    def parent_on(sid, ts):
        last = None
        for t, b in timeline.get(sid, ()):
            if t > ts:
                break
            last = b
        return last == branch

    agents = {}
    for f in subs:
        recs = list(_assistant(f))
        if not recs or (home and _home(recs[0].get("cwd")) != home):
            continue
        first = min(d["timestamp"] for d in recs)
        if not (any(d.get("gitBranch") == branch for d in recs) or parent_on(recs[0].get("sessionId"), first)):
            continue
        try:
            meta = json.load(open(f[:-len(".jsonl")] + ".meta.json"))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            meta = {}
        if meta.get("attributionSkill") in REVIEW_SKILLS or any(d.get("attributionSkill") in REVIEW_SKILLS for d in recs):
            continue
        aid = recs[0].get("agentId") or os.path.basename(f)
        a = agents.setdefault(aid, {"type": meta.get("agentType") or recs[0].get("attributionAgent") or "?", "calls": {}})
        for d in recs:
            a["calls"][d.get("requestId") or d.get("uuid")] = d["message"]["model"]
    per_main = {}
    for model in main.values():
        per_main[model] = per_main.get(model, 0) + 1
    per_agent = {}
    for a in agents.values():
        key = (a["type"], "+".join(sorted(set(a["calls"].values()))))
        x = per_agent.setdefault(key, {"type": key[0], "model": key[1], "agents": 0, "calls": 0})
        x["agents"] += 1
        x["calls"] += len(a["calls"])
    return {"main": per_main, "agents": sorted(per_agent.values(), key=lambda x: (x["type"], x["model"]))}


def by_severity(items, keep=lambda g: True):
    out = {"S1": 0, "S2": 0, "S3": 0, "S?": 0}
    for s, g in items:
        if keep(g):
            out[{2: "S1", 1: "S2", 0: "S3"}.get(s, "S?")] += 1
    return out


# ---------- merge ----------


def exists_note(repo, f):
    if not repo or f["file"] in ("?", ""):
        return None
    path = os.path.join(repo, f["file"])
    if not os.path.isfile(path):
        return "cited file not in the worktree"
    if f["line"]:
        with open(path, errors="replace") as fh:
            n = sum(1 for _ in fh)
        if f["line"] > n:
            return "cited line %d is past the end (%d lines)" % (f["line"], n)
    return None


def merge(rev_text, cr_text, repo, use_model=True, use_shadow=True, base="main"):
    t0 = time.time()
    notes = []
    R, seen = parse_reviewer(rev_text)
    C = parse_code_review(cr_text)
    if C is None:
        notes.append("the /code-review report has no JSON list; read it in full")
        C = []
    if not R and rev_text.strip():
        notes.append("no reviewer finding parsed (no `verdict:` line); read its report in full")
    for i, f in enumerate(R, 1):
        f.update(id="R%d" % i, src="reviewer", file=norm(repo, f["file"]))
    for i, f in enumerate(C, 1):
        f.update(id="C%d" % i, src="code-review", file=norm(repo, f["file"]))
    allf = R + C
    byid = {f["id"]: f for f in allf}
    pairs = [{"id": "%s~%s" % (r["id"], c["id"]), "a": r["id"], "b": c["id"]}
             for r in R for c in C if r["file"] == c["file"]]

    sev, same, cost, model_ok = {}, {}, 0.0, False
    source = os.path.basename(git(repo, "rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir").strip().rstrip("/")
                              .rsplit("/.git", 1)[0]) if repo else None
    row = None
    if use_model and allf:
        try:
            row = gate.resolve("review-gate.merge")
            if row is None:
                notes.append("merge model off in settings/models.json: lists unmerged, severity unknown")
        except gate.GateError as e:
            notes.append("merge model not run (%s): lists unmerged, severity unknown" % str(e)[:160])
    with cf.ThreadPoolExecutor(2) as ex:
        fj = ex.submit(shadow, byid, pairs, source) if use_shadow else None
        if row:
            try:
                sev, same, cost = ask_merge(allf, pairs, repo, row)
                model_ok = True
            except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 — fall back to the two lists, said so
                notes.append("merge model failed (%s): lists unmerged, severity unknown" % str(e)[:160])
        jev, jev_note = fj.result() if fj else ({}, None)
    if jev_note:  # stderr, not a ⚠: a pair Jev did not answer is Opus's, so the parent need not see it
        print("review-gate: " + jev_note, file=sys.stderr)
    taken = took(jev)
    decided = dict(same, **taken)
    if taken and not model_ok:
        # the fallback notes above say "lists unmerged": with Jev's pairs folded in, not quite
        notes = [n.replace("lists unmerged,", "lists unmerged but for Jev's confident pairs,") for n in notes]
        notes.append("Jev's confident pairs merged all the same (%d of %d)" % (len(taken), len(pairs)))

    parent = {f["id"]: f["id"] for f in allf}

    def find(x):
        while parent[x] != x:
            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]
            x = parent[x]
        return x

    for p in pairs:
        try:
            if float(decided.get(p["id"], 0)) >= SAME:
                parent[find(p["b"])] = find(p["a"])
        except (TypeError, ValueError):
            pass
    groups = {}
    for f in allf:
        groups.setdefault(find(f["id"]), []).append(f)

    def s_of(f):
        try:
            return int(sev.get(f["id"]))
        except (TypeError, ValueError):
            return -1

    items = []
    for g in groups.values():
        s = max(s_of(f) for f in g)
        wrong = any(f.get("verdict") == "WRONG" for f in g)
        items.append((-s, not wrong, -len(g), g[0]["file"], g[0]["line"] or 0, g))
    items.sort(key=lambda t: t[:5])

    out = []
    head = "Merged review — %d finding(s): %d from the reviewer, %d from /code-review, %d merged" % (
        len(items), len(R), len(C), len(allf) - len(items))
    if model_ok:
        head += " · %s $%.3f" % (model_label(row), cost)
    if taken:
        head += " · Jev decided %d of %d pair(s)" % (len(taken), len(pairs))
    out.append(head)
    for n in notes:
        out.append("⚠ " + n)
    out.append("")
    for k, t in enumerate(items, 1):
        g = t[-1]
        s = -t[0]
        lab = {2: "S1", 1: "S2", 0: "S3"}.get(s, "S?")
        loc = g[0]["file"] + (":%d" % g[0]["line"] if g[0]["line"] else "")
        both = "reviewer + code-review" if len({f["src"] for f in g}) == 2 else g[0]["src"]
        out.append("%d. %s · %s · %s" % (k, lab, loc, both))
        for f in g:
            tag = (" [%s]" % f["verdict"]) if f.get("verdict") else ""
            where = "" if f is g[0] else " (%s%s)" % (f["file"], ":%d" % f["line"] if f["line"] else "")
            if f.get("cites"):
                where = " (cites %s)" % f["cites"]
            out.append("   - %s%s%s: %s" % (f["src"], tag, where, claim(f)))
            if f.get("evidence"):
                out.append("     evidence: " + f["evidence"])
            if f.get("fix"):
                out.append("     fix: " + f["fix"])
            note = exists_note(repo, f)
            if note:
                out.append("     ⚠ " + note)
        if both == "code-review":
            out.append("     (no evidence line: check it against the code before fixing)")
    groups = [(-t[0], t[-1]) for t in items]
    _log(repo, R, C, pairs, same, jev, cost, model_ok, byid, time.time() - t0, groups, base, taken)
    return "\n".join(out)


def took(jev):
    """{pair id: p} for the pairs Jev decides: answered by a measured version (TAKES), confident."""
    out = {}
    for k, v in jev.items():
        p = v.get("p")
        if v.get("model") in TAKES and isinstance(p, (int, float)) and not CONFIDENT[0] <= p <= CONFIDENT[1]:
            out[k] = p
    return out


def _log(repo, R, C, pairs, same, jev, cost, model_ok, byid, secs, groups=(), base="main", taken=None):
    taken = taken or {}
    try:
        branch = git(repo, "rev-parse", "--abbrev-ref", "HEAD").strip() if repo else None
        git_common = git(repo, "rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir").strip() if repo else ""
        try:
            models = built_by(branch, git_common.rstrip("/").rsplit("/.git", 1)[0] if git_common else None)
        except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 — a transcript we cannot read must not lose the line
            models = {"error": str(e)[:200]}
        rec = {"ts": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z"), "repo": repo, "branch": branch,
               "project": os.path.basename(git_common.rstrip("/").rsplit("/.git", 1)[0]) if git_common else None,
               "diff": diff_size(repo, base) if repo else None,
               "findings": by_severity(groups),
               "wrong": by_severity(groups, lambda g: any(f.get("verdict") == "WRONG" for f in g)),
               "models": models,
               "reviewer": len(R), "code_review": len(C), "opus_ok": model_ok, "opus_usd": round(cost, 5),
               "jev_usd": round(sum(v.get("cost_usd") or 0 for v in jev.values()), 6), "secs": round(secs, 1),
               "jev_took": len(taken),
               "pairs": [{"id": p["id"], "opus": same.get(p["id"]), "jev": jev.get(p["id"], {}).get("p"),
                          "took": "jev" if p["id"] in taken else "opus" if p["id"] in same else None,
                          "jev_label": jev.get(p["id"], {}).get("label"),
                          "jev_model": jev.get(p["id"], {}).get("model"), "jev_error": jev.get(p["id"], {}).get("error"),
                          "a": claim(byid[p["a"]])[:300], "b": claim(byid[p["b"]])[:300]} for p in pairs]}
        log = log_path()
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(log), exist_ok=True)
        with open(log, "a") as fh:
            fh.write(json.dumps(rec, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001
        print("review-gate: log not written (%s)" % e, file=sys.stderr)


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)
    p = sub.add_parser("plan")
    p.add_argument("--base", default="main")
    p.add_argument("--repo", default=os.getcwd())
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    m = sub.add_parser("merge")
    m.add_argument("--reviewer", required=True)
    m.add_argument("--code-review", required=True)
    m.add_argument("--repo", default=os.getcwd())
    m.add_argument("--no-model", action="store_true")
    m.add_argument("--no-shadow", action="store_true")
    m.add_argument("--base", default="main")
    a = ap.parse_args()
    repo = git(a.repo, "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel").strip() or a.repo
    if a.cmd == "plan":
        try:
            r = plan(repo, a.base)
        except gate.GateError as e:
            print("review-gate: plan refused: %s" % e, file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        print(json.dumps(r)) if a.json else print_plan(r)
        return 0
    texts = []
    for f in (a.reviewer, a.code_review):
        try:
            texts.append(open(f, errors="replace").read() if f != "-" else sys.stdin.read())
        except OSError as e:
            print("⚠ cannot read %s (%s): nothing merged; read both reports in full" % (f, e.strerror))
            return 0
    print(merge(texts[0], texts[1], repo, not a.no_model, not a.no_shadow, a.base))
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
